:: StoryTitle
Lantern in the Fog

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "F661FB62-CB12-4DD2-9E34-C9C0016200F8",
  "format": "SugarCube",
  "format-version": "2.37.3",
  "start": "Start"
}

:: StoryStylesheet [stylesheet]
body { background: #101725; color: #eef2ff; }
.passage { max-width: 42rem; line-height: 1.6; }
a, .link-internal, button { color: #fbbf24; }

:: StoryInit
<<set $name to "Traveler", $courage to 0, $keepsake to "nothing", $firefliesSeen to false>>

:: Start
The road disappears into a bank of silver fog.

What should the story call you? Type a name, then press Enter to light the lantern.

<<textbox "$name" "Traveler" "Crossroads" autofocus>>

:: Crossroads
The lantern wakes in $name's hand. Two paths emerge.

[[Follow the fireflies->Grove][$courage += 1]]

[[Enter the old tunnel->Tunnel][$courage += 2]]

:: Grove
Blue fireflies drift between the trees.

<<linkappend "Watch them more closely">>
  <<set $firefliesSeen to true>>
  They arrange themselves into an arrow pointing home.
<</linkappend>>

<<linkreplace "Pick up the silver leaf">>
  <<set $keepsake to "a silver leaf">>
  The leaf is warm despite the cold fog.
<</linkreplace>>

[[Walk toward the distant bell->Ending]]

:: Tunnel
Water taps against the stones. A small chest rests beside the wall.

<<linkreplace "Open the chest">>
  <<set $keepsake to "a brass key">>
  Inside is a brass key engraved with a tiny sunrise.
<</linkreplace>>

[[Climb the stair beyond the chest->Ending]]

:: Ending
The fog thins, and $name steps into morning.

<<if $courage >= 2>>You chose the darker road and found courage there.<<else>>You trusted the lights and found a gentler way through.<</if>>

<<if $keepsake isnot "nothing">>You carry $keepsake with you.<<else>>Your hands are empty, but the lantern is still burning.<</if>>

<<if $firefliesSeen>>Far behind you, the fireflies complete their bright little map.<<endif>>

''The End''

[[Play again->Start][$name = "Traveler"; $courage = 0; $keepsake = "nothing"; $firefliesSeen = false]]
